<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42880" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scăpŭla</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a Roman surname.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A partisan of Pompey</i>, <i>the main
				instigator of the Spanish war</i>, Auct. B. Hisp. 33; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				9, 13, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A usurer in the time of Cicero</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Quint. 4,
			17</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scă-pŭlānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>named after one
				Scapula</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 12, 40, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
